WEBVTT

00:02.049 --> 00:04.487
Hello, so this is gonna
be a very quick demo

00:04.758 --> 00:07.762
of Blend and Alchemy
from Base Note Solutions.

00:07.762 --> 00:11.357
So, this is an implementation of Blend
for our client VEXERA Fragrances.

00:12.128 --> 00:13.550
This is the customer's storefront.

00:13.550 --> 00:15.092
It's just a website where they can learn

00:15.092 --> 00:17.385
more about how the whole process works.

00:17.774 --> 00:19.867
The first step is you take an assessment.

00:19.898 --> 00:22.472
to see what your fragrance
profile would be like.

00:22.472 --> 00:26.470
This is just to give our AI more
context on what the user likes.

00:27.590 --> 00:30.502
Once you save your profile,
you can reserve a spot in the lab,

00:30.533 --> 00:36.394
or you can have an online online
to create a fragrance of your own.

00:36.976 --> 00:39.969
Here you can give it
a natural language prompt

00:39.969 --> 00:41.603
on what type of fragrances you like.

00:42.045 --> 00:45.041
“Something cool and airy.”

00:45.340 --> 00:49.175
I've been very vague; it'll guide me
through it, giving me further questions.

00:49.670 --> 00:52.756
Alternatively, I can give
it a very specific brief,

00:53.083 --> 00:56.629
which will just give me a blend right
away that I can continue in the store.

00:57.957 --> 00:59.461
Once you've confirmed your reservation,

00:59.461 --> 01:01.688
it goes on to this ERP
platform that we've built,

01:01.688 --> 01:02.872
for VEXERA Fragrances,

01:02.872 --> 01:06.559
where they can see users that have
booked times in the store.

01:06.929 --> 01:08.773
Once they walk in, you can check them in,

01:08.773 --> 01:11.209
and then open a consultation for them.

01:11.555 --> 01:13.391
The staff can see their preferences,

01:13.520 --> 01:16.581
as well as context on how
they answered online.

01:16.973 --> 01:20.364
Here, in store, you can create
an even more specific brief.

01:20.454 --> 01:23.498
for the type of fragrance
that the customer is trying to create.

01:24.188 --> 01:27.423
You should be able to explore
fragrance directions,

01:27.534 --> 01:30.761
three ways that the customer
can go moving forward.

01:31.780 --> 01:35.169
And then, it just gets sent
over to production for them

01:35.199 --> 01:39.067
to create the perfumes based
on the blends generated.

01:39.367 --> 01:42.939
So, that's Blend,
and Alchemy is very similar,

01:42.939 --> 01:47.078
but it is more tuned
towards manufacturers.

01:47.190 --> 01:50.779
It's a manufacturing ERP
instead of retail one.

01:51.179 --> 01:54.261
Alchemy Assistant is more
of a market research tool.

01:54.261 --> 01:56.250
alongside Blend creation as well.

01:56.505 --> 02:01.035
You can ask it for three popular
oud perfumes from the UK.

02:01.547 --> 02:04.923
And it will search
our proprietary perfume database

02:05.195 --> 02:09.378
to see what perfumes match up
with what I am looking for.

02:11.006 --> 02:15.302
And then, the other way this tool can
be used, it will give you a blend.

02:16.138 --> 02:18.669
It does deterministic checks on cost,

02:18.669 --> 02:20.591
and then what materials you have in stock,

02:20.591 --> 02:24.617
and then how much it can use
for the regions you want to sell in,

02:24.617 --> 02:26.368
in terms of compliance and regulations.

02:27.872 --> 02:32.918
So here it's given me a blend
of chemicals, instead of here,

02:33.258 --> 02:36.072
it gives you a blend of oils,

02:36.162 --> 02:38.473
perfume oils that we
provide to the store to use.

02:40.008 --> 02:42.209
It'll give instructions on how to make it.

02:42.617 --> 02:45.088
And then it also shows you

02:45.099 --> 02:49.212
the compliance requirements
that it checked it against.

02:49.532 --> 02:51.138
And then if you are missing materials,

02:51.138 --> 02:53.516
it will give you the materials
that you need to purchase.

02:53.672 --> 02:55.406
And our short demo, thank you!
